  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe default styles are currently:\n\n```css\n::picker(select) {\n  position-area: self-block-end span-self-inline-end;\n  position-try-fallbacks:\n    self-block-start span-self-inline-end,\n    self-block-end span-self-inline-start,\n    self-block-start span-self-inline-start;\n}\n```\n\nBut should it be:\n\n```css\n::picker(select) {\n  position-area: self-block-end span-self-inline-end;\n  position-try-fallbacks: \n    flip-block,\n    flip-inline,\n    flip-block flip-inline;\n}\n```\n\nI think this reacts better to developer changes. For example, if the developer does:\n\n```css\n.custom-select::picker(select) {\n  position-area: self-block-start span-self-inline-start;\n  position-try-order: normal;\n}\n```\n\nIn the current system, the picker will never appear `self-block-end span-self-inline-end`, because that's no longer in the set. With my proposal, it would.\n\nAlso:\n\n```css\n.custom-select::picker(select) {\n  margin-block-end: 1em;\n}\n```\n\nThis margin will always be at the block end, which likely isn't what the developer wants when the picker flips position. With my proposal, the margin would also be flipped.\n\nWDYT @mfreed7 @josepharhar @emilio?",
